  "evidence_classification": "contradicts",
  "interpretation": "In the TB-A02 restoration-studio transfer context, the broad generic negative stack outperformed the narrower targeted-constraint clause on the primary targeted_failure_mode_control dimension (5.00 vs 4.00) and on overall mean (5.0000 vs 4.6250). Semantic compliance and technical-defect cleanliness were unchanged at 5.00 in both conditions, while aesthetic quality was 0.50 lower in the targeted condition. The two lower-scoring targeted-condition outputs were penalized for readable environmental signage/poster text; hand-object interaction remained technically clean. This contradicts the tested at-least-as-strong hypothesis in this context and indicates that narrowly scoped constraints can leave adjacent untargeted failure modes exposed.",
  "limitations": [
    "Four replicates per variant are insufficient for a statistical-significance claim.",
    "Only one frozen blind-review score set was used, so inter-rater reliability was not measured.",
    "The exact host model snapshot and reproducible generation seed were unavailable.",
    "The finding is specific to the TB-A02 restoration-studio archetype and should be replicated across other scenes before broader guidance is adopted.",
    "The targeted clause named readable text on archival tags, while the observed failures were readable environmental signage/poster text; the result therefore does not isolate archival-tag text control from broader environmental-text suppression.",
    "The broad control stack covered additional prohibitions such as blur, artifacts, watermark, and logo, so the comparison tests broad generic coverage versus narrow targeted coverage rather than equal-scope wording."
  ],
